From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:24:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: DL MU-MIMO only when we're an MU
 beamformer

mt7915_mcu_sta_muru_tlv() enabled downlink MU-MIMO for a station when
the interface was an HE or VHT MU beamformer, or a VHT MU beamformee.
The last one is about receiving MU-MIMO, which an access point never
does, and hostapd advertises it by default (mu_beamformee), so on 5 GHz
setting mu_beamformer=0 and he_mu_beamformer=0 still left the firmware's
MU-RU scheduler free to group every station for DL MU-MIMO. Only our
beamformer capabilities count now.

The beamformee term came with the capability rework of 655a6c65, next
to a separate clause for HE stations; in station mode every capability
bit is set (c50be0b5), so nothing changes there.

mt7915_test_sta_muru expected the old behaviour; it now checks a VHT MU
beamformee alone leaves DL MU-MIMO off (24/25 without the fix).

Found while adding MilkFlint's MU-MIMO switch, which until now also had
to clear mu_beamformee.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c            | 7 +++++--
 mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 27261502..68711660 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -959,9 +959,12 @@ mt7915_mcu_sta_muru_tlv(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 
 	muru = (struct sta_rec_muru *)tlv;
 
+	/* we send DL MU-MIMO, so it takes our MU beamformer capability; our
+	 * VHT MU beamformee bit (hostapd's mu_beamformee, on by default) is
+	 * about receiving it and doesn't count
+	 */
 	muru->cfg.mimo_dl_en = mvif->cap.he_mu_ebfer ||
-			       mvif->cap.vht_mu_ebfer ||
-			       mvif->cap.vht_mu_ebfee;
+			       mvif->cap.vht_mu_ebfer;
 	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
 		muru->cfg.mimo_ul_en = true;
 	muru->cfg.ofdma_dl_en = true;
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
index 8c7a5f30..a6b644f2 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
@@ -2802,11 +2802,15 @@ static void mt7915_test_sta_muru(struct kunit *test)
 	muru = mt7915_test_muru_tlv(test, &c);
 	KUNIT_ASSERT_NOT_NULL(test, muru);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, muru->cfg.mimo_dl_en);
+	/* being an MU beamformee ourselves doesn't: an AP advertises that by
+	 * default, and it left MU-MIMO on with mu_beamformer=0 and
+	 * he_mu_beamformer=0
+	 */
 	c.mvif->cap.vht_mu_ebfer = false;
 	c.mvif->cap.vht_mu_ebfee = true;
 	muru = mt7915_test_muru_tlv(test, &c);
 	KUNIT_ASSERT_NOT_NULL(test, muru);
-	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, muru->cfg.mimo_dl_en);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, muru->cfg.mimo_dl_en);
 
 	/* a VHT MU beamformee */
 	mt7915_test_vht(c.sta);
